          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "XiA6X",
          "name": "Purpose",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "m1I82",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Purpose",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "Z30eK",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One screen that answers, in this order: what is failing, how much headroom is left, what is running right now, how slow it is, what it cost, and what the traffic looked like. Errors come first and only render when there are rows — a clean period shows no Errors card at all.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "ySQXf",
          "name": "Entry points",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "PcPRv",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Entry points",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "lt8bE",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "/admin/dashboard/#overview — the default page. Sidebar item 1 of 5 in src/admin/public/js/app.js:209. Every error row is a link into the filtered log (openErrorLogs → #logs).",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "s7ZA9",
          "name": "Screens in this band",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "CQ2Jw",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Screens in this band",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "vbl2W",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Overview / Default — the populated page, mirrored at 6cfefe0. Chart INTERIORS are not mirrored: Chart.js draws a scatter and a line, and the .pen layout cannot position individual points. A hand-drawn approximation would look plausible and misrepresent the shipped chart, so both plot areas carry the card chrome and say so. Everything around them — labels, the % ok, the legend, the axis story — is real.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "gskz5",
          "name": "Business rules",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "UrSK7",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Business rules",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "maNao",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "One window, always: every request the pruner has not deleted, bounded at 30 days by pruneOldLogs. There is no period selector — it was removed 2026-09-20 because the table is already bounded and three options gave every figure its own denominator. The page states the window it measured instead. Both charts share one time axis from the oldest surviving request to just past now, marked with a dashed now line. Quiet hours are drawn as zero, not skipped. Auto-refresh every 30s; 'last read HH:MM:SS' in the shell reports the read, not the window.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "otdq2",
          "name": "Copy source",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "MqB2L",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "Copy source",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "F7BCS8",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "src/admin/views/pages/overview.html verbatim. Numbers shown are illustrative; every label, verdict sentence and empty-state string is the code's. Timestamps render in SHELLM_TZ, default America/Mexico_City.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "P2Kx9l",
          "name": "States not drawn",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
          "gap": 6,
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "ia1G8",
              "name": "Heading",
              "fill": "$primary-container",
              "content": "States not drawn",
              "fontFamily": "$font-headline",
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontWeight": "700"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "anChz",
              "name": "Body",
              "fill": "$on-surface-variant",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "content": "Loading ('Loading stats...') and unreachable ('Could not read stats — …') are one-line string swaps on an otherwise empty page — they carry no layout this screen lacks. The no-database answer renders the window line as 'no requests recorded yet' and hides Capacity, Latency and Usage entirely. USAGE LIMIT HIT is a conditional banner above Capacity with its own colours; it is NOT drawn here, because putting it on the happy path would say it is always present — it belongs to an error band this flow does not have yet. Same for the Errors card, which the code hides when the period is clean: drawn here because triage is the reason the page is opened, and its absence is the easier state to imagine.",
              "lineHeight": 1.6,
              "fontFamily": "$font-mono-render",
              "fontSize": 10,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "frame",
          "id": "E1ghK",
          "name": "Open findings",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "layout": "vertical",
